Problem Definition
College students and young professionals often struggle to keep track of their daily minor
expenditures (food, commute, supplies, entertainment). Existing budgeting applications are
either bloated with unnecessary GUI features, require mandatory cloud accounts, or consume
unnecessary system resources.
Solution Overview
A lightweight, terminal-based Personal Expense & Budget Tracker written in pure Python. It
requires zero third-party packages, stores records persistently using local comma-separated
values (csv), performs input validation, computes category-wise summaries, and alerts users
when their monthly spending exceeds an allocated threshold.
